# Rule: the lattice (ADR-149)

Full rule: `.claude/rules/lattice.md`. The short form:

- Tokens and MECHANISMS are shared; SKINS stay copied. `--lat-*` lives on
  `:root` in `app/styles/lattice.css` (loaded from globals.css) and nowhere else.
- A rung is a height on the rail's 13-tick ladder, never a type size. Type rungs
  carry role names.
- One frame recipe, `.lat-frame`: a two-contour evenodd ring on `::before`, inner
  leg `ch − var(--lat-ch-leg)`, corners as `data-cut="tr-bl|tr|bl|none"`. Never
  `tl-br`. A clip cuts a border and never strokes one.
- The ratchet (`tests/lib/lattice-ratchet.test.ts`) counts polygons, off-scale
  spacing, literal font sizes and off-ladder breakpoints per sheet. Only down.
- The lab is `/test/lattice` inside the REAL HUD frame; the capture asserts, the
  jury scores, usability is capped by measurement; one wave is one CSS state.
